fact WorkItem(id: "WI-1122", description: some(value: "EMBEDDER-SUPPLIED HOST FUNCTIONS: a host cannot bind its own carrier's operations today. HOST_FNS in rustland/anthill-core/src/eval/builtins.rs is a CLOSED const slice, host_fn_by_key consults only that, and register_operation_mappings turns an unknown host_fn key into an EvalError::Internal that kills every interpreter built for the program. So an embedder -- anthill-todo, or any other -- CANNOT WRITE an operation_map naming its own functions: a block like\n\n  provides GithubForge language rust\n    artifact \"rustland/anthill-todo/src/forge/gh.rs\"\n    operation_map { create_entry: \"gh_create_entry\", entry_comments: \"gh_entry_comments\" }\n  end\n\nis not constructible as things stand. VERIFIED still true 2026-08-17 (builtins.rs:366 const HOST_FNS, :450 host_fn_by_key, :479 and :568 document the unknown-key refusal).\n\nTHE FIX: host_fn_by_key consults an EMBEDDER-SUPPLIED TABLE alongside its own. The registry must stay CLOSED in the sense WI-876 cares about -- the arity is carried because the registry is closed, and without it a mapping may bind an operation to a host function that cannot take its arguments (measured there: an arity-1 operation bound to a 2-arg host fn loaded clean and failed at runtime). So an embedder entry must carry its arity the same way, and the same arity check must apply to it.\n\nWHY IT IS ITS OWN TICKET, split out of WI-1115 on 2026-08-17. It is anthill-core SUBSTRATE, in a different crate from the WI-437 work, and it is needed by ANY host binding a carrier of its own -- nothing about it is specific to forges, to anthill-todo, or to mirroring. Putting the gh shell-out into anthill-core would fix the symptom in the wrong direction (the kernel would learn about forges), which is exactly why the design named this a prerequisite rather than folding it in (design backend-github-coordination.md §8.3).\n\nFIRST CONSUMER: WI-1117 (export/import), which needs it to bind gh_create_entry and friends. That is a dependency, not a scope: this ticket ships the seam and a test that an embedder-registered function is callable from an operation_map, with the arity check refusing a mismatch. It does NOT ship a forge.\n\nNOT TAGGED wi437 deliberately -- it is not one of that chain's increments, it is a capability the chain happens to need first."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)
